PFE DEV / ARGO CD INCIDENT HANDOFF
Generated: 2026-09-25

Scope
-----
- Argo CD Application: pfe-dev
- Target namespace: pfe-dev
- Git repository: https://github.com/Moatazbench/PFE.git
- Branch / overlay: develop / k8s/overlays/dev

Initial symptoms
----------------
- backend and frontend were Running.
- ai-service was missing from the desired healthy workload state.
- Existing AI Pods were failing with ErrImageNeverPull.
- Argo CD had previously shown Unknown/Degraded because repo-server Git operations timed out.

What was inspected
------------------
- Application, Deployment, ReplicaSets, Pods, Pod events, and Argo logs.
- Git source for develop and k8s/overlays/dev.
- GitHub Actions workflow definition and published Docker image manifests.
- Docker Desktop Kubernetes / registry-mirror runtime.

Root causes found
-----------------
1. AI workload pull policy
   k8s/overlays/dev/ai-service-patch.yaml explicitly set:
     imagePullPolicy: Never

   CI publishes immutable SHA image tags. A newly published tag is not already
   present on the Kubernetes node, so the kubelet cannot start it when its pull
   policy is Never. The exact Pod failure was ErrImageNeverPull.

2. Local Docker Desktop registry mirror
   During recovery the Kubernetes runtime temporarily failed pulls through
   registry-mirror:1273. The image existed in Docker Hub. Restarting Docker
   Desktop and allowing the AI image pull to complete restored the runtime.
   The AI image is large (about 1.34 GB), so its initial pull took several minutes.

3. Argo CD repo-server Git fetches
   Argo repo-server repeatedly runs:
     git fetch origin --tags --force --prune

   The repository object store is approximately 1.34 GB. A shallow clone from
   repo-server succeeds, but the full tagged fetch exceeds repo-server's 90-second
   Git timeout. This leaves Application pfe-dev in Unknown even while the live
   Kubernetes workload is healthy.

Changes made
------------
1. Git source-of-truth fix (committed and pushed)
   Commit: 9b1de60 fix(dev): allow AI service image pull
   File:   k8s/overlays/dev/ai-service-patch.yaml
   Change: imagePullPolicy: Never -> Always

   Render validation confirmed the dev overlay produces:
     image: moatazbench/pfe-ai-service:<immutable SHA>
     imagePullPolicy: Always

2. CI follow-up image update
   GitHub Actions subsequently committed:
     292f2b1 ci: update dev image to 9b1de6072df0cb35934b88d87078c355c84e8ae9

   Docker manifest inspection confirmed that AI image tag exists in the registry.

3. Runtime recovery
   - Refreshed Argo application reconciliation.
   - Restarted Docker Desktop after confirming the embedded Kubernetes registry
     mirror was cancelling image resolution requests.
   - Pulled the AI image successfully and verified ai-service Running.
   - Recovered Argo repo-server Pods after their copyutil init containers were
     crash-looping with: /bin/ln: Already exists
   - Restarted only argocd-repo-server and argocd-application-controller; no
     Deployment, namespace, or Argo CD installation was deleted.
   - Added attempted Argo timeout settings in argocd-cmd-params-cm:
       controller.repo.server.timeout.seconds: "180"
       reposerver.git.request.timeout: "180s"
     Repo-server still logged its internal full-fetch timeout at 90 seconds.

Current verified workload state at last check
---------------------------------------------
- ai-service: 1/1 Running
- backend:    1/1 Running
- frontend:   1/1 Running
- Current running AI image:
    moatazbench/pfe-ai-service:2303a23ec295a398045845da5605481103c5da3f
- Current AI Deployment settings:
    replicas: 1
    imagePullPolicy: Always
- No running ai-service Pod has ErrImageNeverPull.

Current unresolved state
------------------------
- Argo pfe-dev is Healthy but Sync status is Unknown.
- This is caused by repo-server's full tagged Git fetch timing out, not by the
  AI image, AI Deployment replica count, or CI image publication.
- Because Argo cannot complete its full fetch, it has not yet advanced the live
  Deployment to the newer CI-generated 9b1de607... image tag.

Permanent remediation (requires explicit approval)
---------------------------------------------------
The lasting fix is to reduce Git history size:

1. Identify the large blobs and determine which must remain available.
2. Move required large assets/models to Git LFS or a model/artifact registry.
3. Use git-filter-repo (or BFG Repo-Cleaner) to remove the historical large
   blobs from every affected ref.
4. Create backup refs before rewriting history.
5. Force-push rewritten branches/tags to GitHub.
6. All users and CI checkout environments must re-clone the repository.
7. Restart/refresh Argo repo-server and pfe-dev.
8. Verify Git -> Argo CD -> Kubernetes converges to:
     Argo CD: Synced / Healthy
     ai-service: 1/1 Running with latest immutable CI tag
     backend: 1/1 Running
     frontend: 1/1 Running

Why approval is required
------------------------
History rewriting changes commit IDs and requires force-pushing shared branches.
It is intentionally not performed without explicit authorization.

Important do-not-do items
-------------------------
- Do not delete the pfe-dev namespace, AI Deployment, or Argo CD installation.
- Do not blindly run rollout undo.
- Do not set ai-service replicas to 0; intended replicas are 1.
- Do not use imagePullPolicy: Never for CI-published immutable image tags.

Useful verification commands
----------------------------
kubectl get application pfe-dev -n argocd
kubectl get pods -n pfe-dev
kubectl get deployment ai-service -n pfe-dev -o jsonpath='{.spec.replicas} {.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}{"\\n"}'
kubectl get rs -n pfe-dev -l app=ai-service -o wide
kubectl logs -n argocd deploy/argocd-repo-server --tail=200

